      "chatId": "19:5df46302-9f5a-492f-9b81-db865b3c977e_9d7bec55-1d49-4e25-8776-b3a3130088de@unq.gbl.spaces",
      "from": "9d7bec55-1d49-4e25-8776-b3a3130088de",
      "fromDisplayName": "Rajakumar, Kandhan",
      "body": "<p>Test 1: KS_MLCDATAR5_VMIN_K_ENDTC1_STF_CORE_X_F1_SSA \u2014 No DTS data \u2705 Expected<br>\nThis is the Vmin result test. It stores:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Vmin value (pass/fail margin)<br>\nFunctional bin<br>\nIt does NOT store DTS temperature \u2014 by design. The DTS read result for this test lives in:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>KS_MLCDATAR5_VMIN_K_ENDTC1_STF_CORE_X_F1_SSA_DTS</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>That _DTS companion test exists and has data. The two are paired \u2014 same SSID/timestamp. This is working as designed. To get temperature at time of Vmin test, you join _SSA with _SSA_DTS by SSID.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Test 2: KS_MLCC6SR6_VMIN_K_ENDTC1_STF_CORE_X_F1_SSA \u2014 No DTS data \u274c Implementation Gap<br>\nThis is the Vmin test for the MLCC6SR6 pattern (different from MLCDATAR5). Unlike the MLCDATAR5 flow, there is no KS_MLCC6SR6_..._SSA_DTS companion test in the program.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The DTS read call was either:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Never added to the MLCC6SR6 test method template (MTT) \u2014 the MTT for MLC6SR6 doesn't invoke DTS read + log result<br>\nAdded only for MLCDATAR5 as a targeted fix, MLCC6SR6 was missed<br>\nWhy the Two Patterns Behave Differently<br>\nAttribute\u2003\u2003MLCDATAR5\u2003\u2003MLCC6SR6<br>\nVmin test\u2003\u2003_SSA\u2003\u2003_SSA<br>\nDTS companion\u2003\u2003_SSA_DTS \u2705 exists\u2003\u2003_SSA_DTS \u274c missing<br>\nDTS result\u2003\u2003Available\u2003\u2003Not logged<br>\nRoot cause\u2003\u2003None (working)\u2003\u2003MTT missing DTS read call<br>\nThe MLCDATAR5 MTT calls DTS_Read() and logs it as a separate test result named &lt;testname&gt;_DTS. The MLCC6SR6 MTT lacks this call.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Fix<br>\nFor MLCC6SR6 missing DTS companion:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The fix is in the MTPL/MTT for the MLCC6SR6 test method:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Add a DTS_Read() call (post-test measurement) in the MLCC6SR6 flow item or test method template<br>\nLog the result as &lt;testname&gt;_DTS \u2014 matching the naming convention already established for MLCDATAR5<br>\nThe DTS read should occur after the Vmin search completes (post-measurement)<br>\nFor correlation (MLCDATAR5 SSA vs SSA_DTS):</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>To pull the actual DTS temperature at the time of each Vmin test, you need to query both test names and join on SSID (Testing_Session_Seq_Key). The _DTS test result row will contain the temperature, the _SSA test row contains the Vmin margin.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Summary<br>\nTest\u2003\u2003Why no DTS data\u2003\u2003Fix needed<br>\nMLCDATAR5_SSA\u2003\u2003By design \u2014 DTS is in companion _SSA_DTS\u2003\u2003None \u2014 correlate by SSID<br>\nMLCC6SR6_SSA\u2003\u2003MTT missing DTS read + result logging\u2003\u2003Add DTS read in MLCC6SR6 MTT</p>",
      "bodyPreview": "<p>Test 1: KS_MLCDATAR5_VMIN_K_ENDTC1_STF_CORE_X_F1_SSA \u2014 No DTS data \u2705 Expected<br>\nThis is the Vmi...",
